cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ThreatForge in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "ThreatForge: An Automated STRIDE Threat-Model Generator from Code and Architecture Diagrams"
abstract: >-
  ThreatForge ingests a code repository and/or an architecture diagram, recovers
  the system's structure via static analysis, infers trust boundaries, and uses a
  grounded local-LLM reasoner over a STRIDE applicability knowledge base to draft a
  per-component STRIDE threat model with mitigations mapped to named controls
  (OWASP ASVS, NIST SP 800-53, CWE) and risk-based triage. It is a human-in-the-loop
  drafting tool: outputs are reviewable drafts, not security sign-offs.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Choksi"
    given-names: "Krishita Sanjay"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
keywords:
  - threat-modeling
  - STRIDE
  - application-security
  - static-analysis
  - data-flow-diagram
  - trust-boundaries
  - security-by-design
